<title>USA: Coke Enterprises gets merger objections.</title>
<headline>Coke Enterprises gets merger objections.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coca-Cola Enterprises Inc said on Monday that the Merger Task Force of the European Commission has issued a statement of objections regarding the company's acquisition of the Coca-Cola and Cadbury bottling operations in Great Britain.</p>
<p>The statement of objections is in keeping with the commission's review process and, as previously noted by Coca-Cola Enterprises, represents a preliminary analysis of the acquisition and its possible effects on the British soft drink market, the company said.</p>
<p>It is seeking to acquire  Amalgamated Beverages Great Britain Ltd.</p>
<p>As its next step in the review process, Coke Enterprises said, it will submit a written reply to the statement of objections. The commission's final decision regarding the transaction is not expected until late in January of 1997.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
